meta {
  name: Respond (offer myself)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/orders/{{order_id}}/respond
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

docs {
  # Respond — offer myself for an order

  The master answers an order from the feed. This does **not** assign the
  order: several masters may respond to the same one, the order stays
  `pending`, and the **client** picks the winner (`04_orders` → List Order
  Responses → Approve / Reject).

  The client is notified live (`MasterRespondedToOrder` on their channel). The
  master learns the outcome over `private-master.{id}`: `MasterAssigned` when
  approved, `OrderResponseRejected` when turned down, `OrderResponseSuperseded`
  when the client chose someone else, `OrderResponseWithdrawn` when the order
  was cancelled.

  Everything is re-checked server-side, including the distance, because nothing
  stops an app from POSTing an order id it never received in the feed. Orders
  from **By Category** outside the radius (`is_within_radius: false`) are
  rejected here with `out of search radius`.

  After responding the order leaves both feeds and shows up in
  **List My Orders** with `filter=awaiting_response`.

  **Response 201:** `OrderMasterResponseResource`
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "id": 7,
      "order_id": 42,
      "status": "pending",
      "created_at": "2026-08-15T10:05:00+05:00",
      "decided_at": null,
      "rejection_reason": null
    }
  }
  ```

  **Errors (all `422`, message localized by `X-Locale`):**

  | Cause                               | Meaning                                  |
  |-------------------------------------|------------------------------------------|
  | already claimed                     | the order already has a master, or is not `pending` |
  | own order                           | placed from this same account as a client |
  | category mismatch                   | not one of the master's trades            |
  | master location unknown             | no GPS ping yet                           |
  | out of search radius                | too far for the order's current radius    |
  | already responded                   | this master already answered this order   |
  | master unavailable / access expired | switched off, blocked, or unsubscribed    |

  - `404` — order not found
  - `403` — token has no usable master profile (see `reason`)
}
